{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "102", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "\"Oh, darling, you look…comfortable,\" Seraphina said, adjusting the train of her shimmering emerald gown. Her voice was a melodic chime.\n\nLeo pulled his sweatpants higher, tugging at the drawstring. \"And you look like you're about to float away. Seriously, Seraphina, are you sure about this? It's just the monthly board game night at Agnes's.\"\n\nSeraphina gasped dramatically. \"Just board games? Leo, this is *Agnes’s* board game night! It’s a tradition! There’s artisanal cheese, obscure card games, and Beatrice always brings her prize-winning cucumber sandwiches.\"\n\nLeo sighed. \"Right. Cucumber sandwiches. Look, I'm happy for you to go and… sparkle. I’m just not feeling the whole ball gown vibe for a game of Clue.\"\n\n\"But it's *important* to make an effort!\" Seraphina insisted, smoothing her skirt. \"It's about showing respect for the occasion, for Agnes, for the *spirit* of competitive tabletop entertainment!\"\n\nLeo chuckled. \"The spirit of competitive tabletop entertainment? You're something else. I’ll be there, mostly to provide moral support and strategically place snacks.\"\n\n* He really doesn't understand the nuances of high society gatherings.\n* I need to remember to compliment Agnes's new hat.\n* I hope Beatrice doesn't try to explain the rules of Mahjong again.\n\n\n\n\"Well, try to at least *attempt* a smile,\" Seraphina instructed, giving his arm a light squeeze. \"And for heaven's sake, try to look less like you're ready for a marathon.\"\n\nLeo grinned. \"No promises. But I’ll bring the dice.\"\n\nSeraphina beamed. \"Wonderful! Now, let’s go. The early bird gets the best cucumber sandwiches.\"\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.06885108351707458}, {"token": "Oh", "logprob": -0.20756588876247406}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.1734156757593155}, {"token": "▁darling", "logprob": -0.052139732986688614}, {"token":